<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2015/Piletina.jpg" alt="Piletina is a Croatian word for chicken" width="450" height="433" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Piletina. 12x12, oil on linen panel. 2015.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">More than anything else, I wanted this painting to be about the light and the way it varied in intensity from top to bottom and front to back. My starting point was a reference photo taken last year. There was out-of-focus chicken wire in the foreground which changed some of the values in interesting ways.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I had originally meant to leave part of the canvas unpainted but as I got nearer to completion it was clear that this wasn't working. I fixed that problem while the paint was still wet.&nbsp;<span style="line-height: 1.42857143;">One important lesson I've learned is that mixtures using burnt umber (like this background) darken as they dry and it is nearly impossible to re-create the same shade and value at a later date.</span></p>